  "annotation": {
    "schema_version": 5,
    "type": "new architecture support",
    "problem": [
      {
        "text": "Mixtral was mentioned as planned support, but the parent architecture registry had no MixtralForCausalLM entry; directory-based configuration dispatch would reject it.",
        "basis": "source",
        "evidence": [
          "call_3564ee4ae2e4408180b4c2282671dbe0",
          "call_a60baf5e46d9457493212e576677bd0a",
          "call_fcd8805d821a46bb90b485a0b5632e8f"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "reasoning": [
      {
        "text": "The change supplies Mixtral-specific configuration and checkpoint-key mappings while reusing existing attention, transformer blocks and routed-expert execution. Registration and the new classes work together: the registry derives its dispatch key from MixtralConfig.arch_string.",
        "basis": "source",
        "evidence": [
          "call_baad383a78ab49189623a17995834fb2",
          "call_9db0e1ecb9f0495d913ba981c2f5844e",
          "call_a60baf5e46d9457493212e576677bd0a"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "impact": [
      {
        "text": "Config.from_directory can now select MixtralConfig, and Model.from_config can instantiate MixtralModel. This establishes an assembly path, not measured checkpoint-loading or generation success.",
        "basis": "source",
        "evidence": [
          "call_fcd8805d821a46bb90b485a0b5632e8f",
          "call_25a17435c16e4b8e993acff257fd6eef",
          "call_9db0e1ecb9f0495d913ba981c2f5844e",
          "call_baad383a78ab49189623a17995834fb2"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "source_notes": [
      {
        "text": "The Qwen3 MoE ancestor entry was read. It describes the closely related model assembly, all-expert calibration policy and a conditional fused-path shape mismatch.",
        "basis": "ancestor",
        "evidence": [
          "call_8d9d7d804ca64912ab0b3c9ada7fda92"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "PR #4, \u201cchore: update config.py,\u201d proposes a spelling correction. Issue #7, \u201cquantizing model: undefined symbol: __cxa_call_terminate,\u201d reports extension loading. Their relevance here is inferred only from the shared configuration file, not an explicit relationship to Mixtral support.",
        "basis": "inference",
        "evidence": [
          "call_ee87130eca5649d1865ded83292497bb",
          "call_b14b699f1e3145838a3c6543d42e3e3a",
          "call_fcd8805d821a46bb90b485a0b5632e8f"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Issue #33, \u201cError converting model,\u201d initially reports file-opening failure and later discusses GLM output; #34, \u201ctorch._C._LinAlgError on last layer of quant,\u201d reports Cholesky failure; #38, \u201cError converting nvidia/Llama-3_1-Nemotron-Ultra-253B-v1,\u201d reports a sliced-loading dimension mismatch. Any association with this task is inferred solely from their shared convert_model.py path; none establishes a Mixtral failure.",
        "basis": "inference",
