    "chapters": [
      {
        "id": "models",
        "title": "Mixtral registration and routed-expert assembly",
        "claims": [
          {
            "text": "MixtralConfig maps intermediate_size to moe_intermediate_size and num_local_experts to num_experts, unlike Qwen3 MoE's moe_intermediate_size and num_experts configuration keys. num_experts_per_tok remains the routing cardinality. A supplied hidden_act must be silu, although omission is allowed.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_9db0e1ecb9f0495d913ba981c2f5844e",
              "call_90591634815742eaa9b70ef62d8134bb",
              "call_fcd8805d821a46bb90b485a0b5632e8f",
              "call_3313b805f38b4a15bbec3390dc2a531f",
              "call_6f2e3690ab27498d9bf2b3e7275f29f4",
              "call_980c74d5bff6469fa048a8fbc7fa7254"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Head dimension uses the explicit head_dim when truthy, otherwise hidden_size // num_attention_heads. KV heads default to query heads, and tied embeddings default to false. RoPE uses the shared configuration reader with NEOX style.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_9db0e1ecb9f0495d913ba981c2f5844e",
              "call_fcd8805d821a46bb90b485a0b5632e8f"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The model assembles an embedding, one sequential pre-normalized TransformerBlock per layer, final RMSNorm and vocabulary projection. Each block adds attention to its residual before normalizing for the MLP and adding that result. Attention uses separate q_proj/k_proj/v_proj/o_proj tensors, without Q/K normalization or an explicit sliding window.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_9db0e1ecb9f0495d913ba981c2f5844e",
              "call_04bcb961098246cda437429eb3ef3cab",
              "call_d369e1a2290344d799e9294d4006d9ab"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Under model.layers.{idx}.block_sparse_moe, gate is the router and expert w1/w3/w2 are respectively gate/up/down projections. BlockSparseMLP computes softmax routing, selects and renormalizes top-k weights, then accumulates weighted down(SiLU(gate(x)) \u00d7 up(x)). Mixtral requests half-precision intermediates and outputs. The router uses pad_to=1, preserving exactly num_experts outputs.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_9db0e1ecb9f0495d913ba981c2f5844e",
              "call_5ed61e047df345db88ccabcf2cea706a"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Multiple flattened tokens or non-fully-EXL3 experts take the expert-grouped path. A single token with all EXL3 projections takes indexed multi-GEMMs. Fusion requires equal projection dimensions and bit widths within each group, no biases or softcaps, and unit post-scaling. Reuse therefore inherits these preconditions rather than adding a Mixtral-specific kernel.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_5ed61e047df345db88ccabcf2cea706a"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Unlike Qwen3MoeModel, MixtralModel does not enable calibration_all_experts; it retains Model's false default. Conversion forwards that value during capture, so Mixtral calibration uses ordinary selected-expert routing rather than Qwen3 MoE's all-expert capture policy.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_9db0e1ecb9f0495d913ba981c2f5844e",
              "call_90591634815742eaa9b70ef62d8134bb",
              "call_25a17435c16e4b8e993acff257fd6eef",
              "call_a68997c5dfc74c0ca80481d0c900e0a9",
              "call_2702ab39be80411a9f97a0187bd5b567"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The final head can fall back to model.embed_tokens when tying is enabled and lm_head is absent. prepare_inputs stores input_ids and delegates to shared attention preparation, whose default is uncached FlashAttention and whose cached mode prepares cache positions and block tables.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_9db0e1ecb9f0495d913ba981c2f5844e",
              "call_d369e1a2290344d799e9294d4006d9ab"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "mistralai/Mixtral-8x7B-v0.1 and mistralai/Mixtral-8x7B-Instruct-v0.1 each match the registration and key mappings: hidden size 4096, intermediate size 14336, 32 layers, 32 query heads, eight KV heads, eight experts and two selected experts. Both omit head_dim, specify SiLU, untied embeddings, null sliding_window, RMS epsilon 1e-5 and RoPE theta 1,000,000; vocabulary size is 32000.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_b692fbfb383549a6be3d3278ffc3fa86",
              "call_0b65dda417ab4ae6abf296690261c6b1",
              "call_9db0e1ecb9f0495d913ba981c2f5844e"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "mistralai/Mixtral-8x22B-v0.1 and mistralai/Mixtral-8x22B-Instruct-v0.1 each match the mappings with hidden size 6144, intermediate size 16384, 56 layers, 48 query heads, eight KV heads, eight experts and two selected experts. Both omit head_dim and specify the same activation, tying, window, epsilon and theta choices as the 8x7B configurations. Base vocabulary size is 32000; Instruct uses 32768. All four configurations advertise bfloat16, whereas this builder explicitly requests half precision for expert intermediates and outputs.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_a379374e9d464ea5bfde3bc5cf27dc4a",
              "call_1012b9b5739f41fa8ef8c5b8afb5d1c0",
              "call_b692fbfb383549a6be3d3278ffc3fa86",
              "call_0b65dda417ab4ae6abf296690261c6b1",
              "call_9db0e1ecb9f0495d913ba981c2f5844e"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "A standard-library arithmetic check gives fallback head dimension 128 for both sizes, KV projection width 1024, and query widths 4096/6144. This yields four/six query heads per KV head. Two selected experts out of eight is 25% of the expert set, not a measured fraction of total inference work.",
            "basis": "execution",
            "evidence": [
              "call_448c9c4b827d4918b2e4975a0cfc83fd"
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "findings": [
      {
        "id": "inherited-all-expert-fused-shape",
        "origin": "authoring_observation",
        "status": "suspected",
        "classification": "defect",
        "description": "The newly connected Mixtral assembly carries over BlockSparseMLP's conditional mismatch between all-expert routing and fused buffer sizes.",
        "trigger": "One flattened token, fully EXL3 expert projections, activate_all_experts=True, and num_experts different from num_experts_per_tok.",
        "expected_behavior": "Evaluate all requested experts using matching buffers or the expert-grouped path.",
        "actual_behavior": "Routing produces num_experts indices, but fused buffers retain num_experts_per_tok entries. exl3_mgemm checks those dimensions for equality: the inspected Mixtral configurations produce eight versus two. The task does not modify this implementation. Parent caller search found TransformerBlock.forward and ParallelDecoderBlock.forward forwarding params to their MLP; Mixtral uses TransformerBlock. Mixtral's default conversion policy does not set the triggering flag true, so this is not evidence that ordinary conversion fails.",
        "locations": [
          {
